ender', 'full-read', 'preliminary', NULL, 'PDF p. 3, item 2.3 prints "Doorway clearance is 850mm when the door is in the open 90 degree position" in blue, its Code (required) colour. Comparator >=: the source writes "is", and its page 1 calls the code "the minimum standards for accessibility", so the figure is a floor. Lens MOB, access need A-REACH and ICF d465 rest on the source''s PDF p. 1 sentence "a wider turning radius and wider doors are required by many wheelchairs and scooters today", which names exactly door width and turning space: MOB for the wheelchair and scooter users it names; A-REACH because that need''s design obligation names "doorway/turning clearance" and it absorbs wheelchair users; d465 "Moving around using equipment" because the sentence names wheelchairs and scooters. [ASSUMPTION] that a page-1 sentence naming these two quantities warrants their figures elsewhere in the document; a stricter reading of the lens writer''s D-2 rule (the figure''s own words) would move them under the owner''s open question OD-47.', '2026-11-13 22:59', 'session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass', '2026-11-13 22:59', 'session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass', 'claim', '>=', 0, NULL);
