ts above the code figure. The source pairs it with the 850 mm figure; no relation kind in extraction_relations states that pairing (exceeds says the referent is more than needed, the reverse of the source), so no edge is written and the pairing is parked. Lens MOB, access need A-REACH and ICF d465 rest on the source''s PDF p. 1 sentence "a wider turning radius and wider doors are required by many wheelchairs and scooters today", which names exactly door width and turning space: MOB for the wheelchair and scooter users it names; A-REACH because that need''s design obligation names "doorway/turning clearance" and it absorbs wheelchair users; d465 "Moving around using equipment" because the sentence names wheelchairs and scooters. [ASSUMPTION] that a page-1 sentence naming these two quantities warrants their figures elsewhere in the document; a stricter reading of the lens writer''s D-2 rule (the figure''s own words) would move them under the owner''s open question OD-47.', '2026-11-13 23:00', 'session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass', '2026-11-13 23:00', 'session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass', 'claim', '>=', 0, NULL);
