. Comparator >=: a preferred dimension is read as a floor. The source calls a 1500 x 1500 mm square a "turning radius": stored as the side of the square, 1500 mm, as canonical extraction 211 stores a 1.4 m x 1.4 m space as 1.4 m (select ref_id, setting from source_value_extractions where extraction_id=211). Whether 1500 is a radius, a diameter or the side of a square is ambiguous as printed; no follow-up reason holds that (a gap names it). Lens MOB, access need A-REACH and ICF d465 rest on the source''s PDF p. 1 sentence "a wider turning radius and wider doors are required by many wheelchairs and scooters today", which names exactly door width and turning space: MOB for the wheelchair and scooter users it names; A-REACH because that need''s design obligation names "doorway/turning clearance" and it absorbs wheelchair users; d465 "Moving around using equipment" because the sentence names wheelchairs and scooters. [ASSUMPTION] that a page-1 sentence naming these two quantities warrants their figures elsewhere in the document; a stricter reading of the lens writer''s D-2 rule (the figure''s own words) would move them under the owner''s open question OD-47.', '2026-11-13 23:00', 'session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass', '2026-11-13 23:00', 'session_2026-11-13-edmonton-checklist-pass', 'claim', '>=', 0, NULL);
